#. Tag: title
#: glossary.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "Pojmovnik"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this chapter you will find an explanation of most of the <quote>uncommon</"
"quote> words that are used in the handbook."
msgstr ""
"U ovo odjelku će te naći obajšnjenje za večinu <quote>neobičnih</"
"quote>riječi koje su korištene u priručniku."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: glossary.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "degrees"
msgstr "stepeni"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Degrees are units to measure angles or turns. A full turn is 360 degrees, a "
"half turn 180 degrees and a quarter turn 90 degrees. The commands "
"<userinput>turnleft</userinput>, <userinput>turnright</userinput> and "
"<userinput>direction</userinput> need an input in degrees."
msgstr ""
"Stepeni su mjera pomoću koje mjerimo uglove ili krugove. Puni krug je 360 "
"stepeni, polukrug 180 stepeni, ačetvrtnia 90 stepeni. Komande  "
"<userinput>lijevo</userinput>, <userinput>desno</userinput> i "
"<userinput>smjer</userinput> zahtjevaju stepene na ulazu."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: glossary.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "input and output of commands"
msgstr "ulazne i izlazne komande"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some commands take input, some commands give output, some commands take "
"input <emphasis>and</emphasis> give output and some commands neither take "
"input nor give output."
msgstr ""
"Neke komande primaju informacije na ulazu, neke komande daju informacije na "
"izlazu, a neke komande i primaju <emphasis>i</emphasis> daju informacije dok "
"neke ne rade ni jedno."

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some examples of commands that only take input are: <screen>\n"
"forward 50\n"
"pencolor 255,0,0\n"
"print \"Hello!\"\n"
"</screen> The <userinput>forward</userinput> command takes <userinput>50</"
"userinput> as input. <userinput>forward</userinput> needs this input to know "
"how many <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> it should go "
"forward. <userinput>pencolor</userinput> takes a color as input and "
"<userinput>print</userinput> takes a string (a piece of text) as input. "
"Please note that the input can also be a container. The next example "
"illustrates this:"
msgstr ""
"Neki primjeri komandi koje primaju informacije su: <screen>\n"
"naprijed 50\n"
"bojaolovke 255,0,0\n"
"odštampaj \"Hello!\"\n"
"</screen> <userinput>naprijed</userinput> komanda prima <userinput>50</"
"userinput> kao ulaznu informaciju. <userinput>naprijed</userinput> treba ova "
"ulazna informacija da bi znala koliko <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">piksela</"
"glossterm> naprijed da pređe. <userinput>bojaolovke</userinput> prima boju "
"kao argument i <userinput>odštampaj</userinput> uzima string (dio teksta) "
"kao ulazni argument. Primjetite da ulazni argument može biti i kontejner. "
"Slijedeći primjeri ovo oslikavaju:"

#. Tag: screen
#: glossary.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$x = 50\n"
"print $x\n"
"forward 50\n"
"$str = \"hello!\"\n"
"print $str"
msgstr ""
"$x = 50\n"
"odštampaj $x\n"
"naprijed 50\n"
"$str = \"hello!\"\n"
"odštampaj $str"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now some examples of commands that give output: <screen>\n"
"$x = ask \"Please type something and press OK... thanks!\"\n"
"$r = random 1,100\n"
"</screen> The <userinput>ask</userinput> command takes a string as input, "
"and outputs the number or string that is entered. As you can see, the output "
"of <userinput>ask</userinput> is stored in the container <userinput>x</"
"userinput>. The <userinput>random</userinput> command also gives output. In "
"this case it outputs a number between 1 and 100. The output of the random is "
"again stored in a container, named <userinput>r</userinput>. Note that the "
"containers <userinput>x</userinput> and <userinput>r</userinput> are not "
"used in the example code above."
msgstr ""
"Sada neki primjeri koji daju izlazne infromacije: <screen>\n"
"$x = pitaj \"Please type something and press OK... thanks!\"\n"
"$r = nasumično 1,100\n"
"</screen> <userinput>pitaj</userinput> komanda uzima sting kao ulaznu "
"informaciju, i daje broj ili string koji je unesen kao izlaznu informaciju. "
"Kao što možete videjeti <userinput>pitaj</userinput> se nalazi u kontejneru "
"<userinput>x</userinput>. <userinput>nasumično</userinput> kamanda nam "
"također daje izlaznu informaciju. U ovom slučaju broj od 1 do 100. Izlazna "
"informacija ove komande je također spremljena u kontejner, nazvan "
"<userinput>r</userinput>. Primjetite da kontejneri <userinput>x</userinput> "
"i <userinput>r</userinput> nisu korišteni u primjeru gornjeg koda."

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are also commands that neither need input nor give output. Here are "
"some examples:"
msgstr ""
"Postoje komande koje ne trebaju niti ulaz niti daju izlaz. Evo par primjera:"

#. Tag: screen
#: glossary.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"clear\n"
"penup"
msgstr ""
"očisti\n"
"podigniolovku"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: glossary.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "intuitive highlighting"
msgstr "intuitivno naglašavanje"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a feature of &kturtle; that makes coding even easier. With intuitive "
"highlighting the code that you write gets a color that indicates what type "
"of code it is. In the next list you will find the different types of code "
"and the color they get in <link linkend=\"the-editor\">the editor</link>."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je mogućnost &kturtle; koja olakšava kodiranje. Sa intuitivnim "
"označavanjem kod koji pišete dobija boju koja odgovara tipu vašeg koda. U "
"narednoj listi naći će te drugačije tipove koda i boje koje dobivaju u <link "
"linkend=\"the-editor\">uređivaču</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: glossary.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid "Different types of code and their highlight color"
msgstr "Različi tipovi koda i njihova boja označavanja"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "regular commands"
msgstr "obične komande"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "dark blue"
msgstr "tamno plava"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The regular commands are described <link linkend=\"commands\">here</link>."
msgstr "Obične komande su opisane <link linkend=\"commands\">Ovdje</link>."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "execution controlling commands"
msgstr "komande koje upravljaju izvršenjem"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "black (bold)"
msgstr "crno (podebjano)"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These special commands control execution, read more on them <link linkend="
"\"controlling-execution\">here</link>."
msgstr ""
"O ovim posebne komandam koje upravljaju izvršavanjem možete naći više <link "
"linkend=\"controlling-execution\">ovdje</link>."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "comments"
msgstr "komentari"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:48 glossary.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "gray"
msgstr "sivo"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Lines that are commented start with a comment characters (#). These lines "
"are ignored when the code is executed. Comments allow the programmer to "
"explain a bit about his code or can be used to temporarily prevent a certain "
"piece of code from executing."
msgstr ""
"Linije koje su komentirane počinju sa (#). Ove linije se ignorišu kada se "
"kod izvršava. Komentari omogučavaju programeru da bolje objasni svoj kod ili "
"da se privremeno spriječi dio kad pri izvršavanju."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "brackets {, }"
msgstr "zagrade {, }"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "dark green (bold)"
msgstr "tamno zeleno (podebljano)"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Brackets are used to group portions of code. Brackets are often used "
"together with <link linkend=\"controlling-execution\">execution controllers</"
"link>."
msgstr ""
"Zagrade se koriste za grupisanje dijelova kod. One se često koriste sa <link "
"linkend=\"controlling-execution\">upravljačima izvršenja</link>."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <link linkend=\"learn\">learn</link> command"
msgstr "<link linkend=\"learn\">uči</link> komanda"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "light green (bold)"
msgstr "svijtlo zeleno (podebljano)"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <link linkend=\"learn\">learn</link> command is used to create new "
"commands."
msgstr ""
"<link linkend=\"learn\">learn</link> komanda se koristi za pravljenje novih "
"komandi."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "strings"
msgstr "stringovi"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:63 glossary.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "<entry>red</entry>"
msgstr "<entry>crveno</entry>"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Not much to say about (text) strings either, except that they always start "
"and end with the double quotes (\")."
msgstr ""
"O stingovima (tektu) se nema nešto naročito reći, osim da počinju i "
"žavršavaju duplim navodnicima (\")."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "numbers"
msgstr "brojevi"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:68 glossary.docbook:73 glossary.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "dark red"
msgstr "tamno crveno"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numbers, well not much to say about them."
msgstr "Brojevi, o njima nemamo šta reći."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "boolean values"
msgstr "bulove vrijednosti"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are exactly two boolean values, namely: true and false."
msgstr "Postoje samo dvije bulove vrijednosti, respektivno: tačno i netačno."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "variables"
msgstr "promjenljive"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "purple"
msgstr "ljubičasto"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start with a '$' and can contain numbers, strings or boolean values."
msgstr ""
"Počinje sa '$' i može sadržati brojeve, stringove ili bulove vrijednosti."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "mathematical operators"
msgstr "matematički operatori"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the mathematical operators: <userinput>+</userinput>, <userinput>-"
"</userinput>, <userinput>*</userinput>, <userinput>/</userinput> and "
"<userinput>^</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Ovo su matematički operatori: <userinput>+</userinput>, <userinput>-</"
"userinput>, <userinput>*</userinput>, <userinput>/</userinput> i "
"<userinput>^</userinput>."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "comparison operators"
msgstr "upoređivački operatori"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "light blue (bold)"
msgstr "svijetlo plava (podebljano)"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the comparison operators: <userinput>==</userinput>, <userinput>!"
"=</userinput>, <userinput>&lt;</userinput>, <userinput>&gt;</userinput>, "
"<userinput>&lt;=</userinput> and <userinput>&gt;=</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Ovo su upoređujući operatori: <userinput>==</userinput>, <userinput>!=</"
"userinput>, <userinput>&lt;</userinput>, <userinput>&gt;</userinput>, "
"<userinput>&lt;=</userinput> i <userinput>&gt;=</userinput>."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "boolean operators"
msgstr "bulovi operatori"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "pink (bold)"
msgstr "roze (podebljano)"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the boolean operators: <userinput>and</userinput>, <userinput>or</"
"userinput> and <userinput>not</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Ovo su bulovi operatori: <userinput>i</userinput>, <userinput>ili</"
"userinput> i <userinput>ne</userinput>."

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "regular text"
msgstr "običan tekst"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:98 glossary.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "black"
msgstr "crno"

#. Tag: glossterm
#: glossary.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "pixels"
msgstr "pikseli"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A pixel is a dot on the screen. If you look very close you will see that the "
"screen of your monitor uses pixels. All images on the screen are built with "
"these pixels. A pixel is the smallest thing that can be drawn on the screen."
msgstr ""
"Piksel je tačka na zaslonu. Ako pogledate pažljivo videjti će te da ekran "
"koristi piksele. Sve slike na zaslonu su sačinjene od piksela. Piksel je "
"najmanja stvar koju možete nacrtati na zaslonu."

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A lot of commands need a number of pixels as input. These commands are: "
"<userinput>forward</userinput>, <userinput>backward</userinput>, "
"<userinput>go</userinput>, <userinput>gox</userinput>, <userinput>goy</"
"userinput>, <userinput>canvassize</userinput> and <userinput>penwidth</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Veliki broj komandi zahtjeva broj piksela kao ulaznu informaciju. Ove "
"komande su: <userinput>naprijed</userinput>, <userinput>nazad</userinput>, "
"<userinput>idi</userinput>, <userinput>idipox</userinput>, "
"<userinput>idipoy</userinput>, <userinput>veličinaplatna</userinput> i "
"<userinput>debljinaolovke</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In early versions of &kturtle; the canvas was essentially a raster image, "
"yet for recent versions the canvas is a vector drawing. This means that the "
"canvas can be zoomed in and out, therefore a pixel does not necessarily have "
"to translate to one dot on the screen."
msgstr ""
"U ranim verzijama &kturtle; platno je bilo slika od niza linija, dok je "
"danas vektorska slika. To znači da možemo približiti i udaljiti platno, "
"stoga piksel ne mora nužno biti preveden u samo jednu tačku na ekranu."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: glossary.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "RGB combinations (color codes)"
msgstr "RGB kombincije (kodovi boja)"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"RGB combinations are used to describe colors. The <quote>R</quote> stand for "
"<quote>red</quote>, the <quote>G</quote> stands for <quote>green</quote> and "
"the <quote>B</quote> stands for <quote>blue</quote>. An example of an RGB "
"combination is <userinput>255,0,0</userinput>: the first value (<quote>red</"
"quote>) is 255 and the others are 0, so this represents a bright shade of "
"red. Each value of an RGB combination has to be in the range 0 to 255. Here "
"a small list of some often used colors:"
msgstr ""
"RGB kombinacije se koriste za opisivanje boja.  <quote>R</quote> označava "
"<quote>crvenu</quote>, <quote>G</quote> označava <quote>zelenu</quote> i "
"<quote>B</quote> označava <quote>plavu</quote>. Primjer RGB kombinacije je "
"<userinput>255,0,0</userinput>: prva vrijednost (<quote>crvena</quote>) je "
"255 dok su ostale 0, te je ovo rezultiralo jarkom crvenom bojom. Svaka "
"vrijednost RGB kombinacije ima vrijednost od 0 do 255. Evo male liste nekih "
"često korištenih:"

#. Tag: title
#: glossary.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Often used RGB combinations"
msgstr "Često korištene RGB kombinacije"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "0,0,0"
msgstr "0,0,0"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "255,255,255"
msgstr "255,255,255"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "white"
msgstr "bijelo"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "255,0,0"
msgstr "255,0,0"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "150,0,0"
msgstr "150,0,0"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "0,255,0"
msgstr "0,255,0"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "green"
msgstr "zeleno"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "0,0,255"
msgstr "0,0,255"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "blue"
msgstr "plavo"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "0,255,255"
msgstr "0,255,255"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "light blue"
msgstr "svijetlo plavo"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "255,0,255"
msgstr "255,0,255"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "pink"
msgstr "roze"

#. Tag: userinput
#: glossary.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "255,255,0"
msgstr "255,255,0"

#. Tag: entry
#: glossary.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "yellow"
msgstr "žuto"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Two commands need an RGB combination as input: these commands are "
"<userinput>canvascolor</userinput> and <userinput>pencolor</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Dvije komande trebaju RGB kombinaciju kao ulaz: ove komande su "
"<userinput>bojaplatna</userinput> i <userinput>bojaolovke</userinput>."

#. Tag: glossterm
#: glossary.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "sprite"
msgstr "grafika"

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A sprite is a small picture that can be moved around the screen. Our beloved "
"turtle, for instance, is a sprite."
msgstr ""
"Grafika je mala slika koja se može pomjerati po zaslonu. Naša voljena "
"konjača, npr. je grafika."

#. Tag: para
#: glossary.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note: with this version of &kturtle; the sprite cannot be changed from a "
"turtle into something else. Future versions of &kturtle; will be able to do "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Bilješka: sa ovom verzijom &kturtle; grafika može postati nešto drugo osim "
"kornajče. Buduće verzije &kturtle; će također imati ovu mogućnost."
